<law>
	<structure>
		<unit label="title" identifier="4.1" level="1">Alcoholic Beverage and Cannabis Control</unit>
		<unit label="subtitle" identifier="I" level="2">Alcoholic Beverage Control Act</unit>
		<unit label="chapter" identifier="3" level="3">Prohibited Practices; Penalties; Procedural Matters</unit>
		<unit label="article" identifier="1" level="4">Prohibited Practices Generally</unit>
	</structure>
	<section_number>4.1-301</section_number>
	<catch_line>Conspiracy to violate § 4.1-300; penalty</catch_line>
	<text>
		If two or more persons conspire together to do any act which is in violation of § 4.1-300, and one or more of these persons does any act to effect the object of the conspiracy, each of the parties to such conspiracy shall be guilty of a Class 6 felony.
	</text>
	<history>1956, c. 70, § 4-57.1; 1993, c. 866.</history>
</law>
